# Project Architecture

This repository is a Turborepo monorepo.

Applications:

apps/

- website
- admin
- backend

Shared packages:

packages/

- shared-types
- eslint-config
- prettier-config

Documentation:

docs/

Assets:

assets/

---

# Architectural Principles

Always follow:

- Clean Architecture
- SOLID
- DRY
- KISS
- Feature-Based Organization
- Separation of Concerns
- Dependency Inversion
- Composition over Inheritance

---

# Never

Never duplicate business logic.

Never duplicate components.

Never create circular dependencies.

Never bypass Service Layer.

Never access database directly from controllers.

Never expose internal implementation details.

---

# Dependency Direction

Frontend

↓

API

↓

Service Layer

↓

Repository

↓

Database

Never invert this dependency.

---

# Folder Responsibility

Website

Responsible only for:

- Public pages
- Customer experience
- Marketing
- Reservation UI
- Membership UI
- Loyalty UI

Admin

Responsible only for:

- CMS
- Dashboard
- Analytics
- User Management
- Reservation Management
- Loyalty Management
- Reports

Backend

Responsible only for:

- Business Logic
- API
- Authentication
- Authorization
- Database
- File Storage
- Background Jobs

---

# Shared Code

Only place code in packages if:

It is used by two or more applications.

Otherwise keep it local.

---

# Configuration

Environment variables must never be hardcoded.

Always use configuration files.

---

# API

REST API

/api/v1

Future versions:

/api/v2

---

# Database

Single PostgreSQL database.

Redis for cache.

MinIO for object storage (future).

---

# Scalability

Design every feature assuming:

Multi-branch cafes

Thousands of users

Multiple administrators

Multiple concurrent reservations

Future POS integration

Future mobile applications

Future payment gateway

Future inventory system

---

# Definition of Good Architecture

Easy to read.

Easy to extend.

Easy to test.

Easy to maintain.

Easy to deploy.

Easy to scale.